# The Telemetry Logs page: tableLayoutPaneltlogs. A tlog plays in the time it was recorded in,
# divided by the speed a button sets (BUT_speed1_Click: 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 1x, 2x, 5x, 10x, said on
# lbl_playbackspeed as "x " and the speed); Play/Pause toggles it (BUT_playlog_Click, the button
# reading "Pause" while it plays and "Play" when not); the end of the file stops it; and the track
# bar moves the file to its percentage (tracklog_Scroll), a press beside the thumb moving it by its
# LargeChange, 5, with lbl_logpercent saying where the file is.
# `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:556-594, 1674-1678, 3474-3568, 5361-5378, 5543-5577, 5630-5660,
# GCSViews/FlightData.Designer.cs:2193-2320`
#
# Plays the recorded copter flight - 36 seconds of it - so it needs no vehicle. Run from the
# repository root:
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-playback.gui -- file:testdata/mavlink/autotest.tlog

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 16

# Telemetry Logs is the thirteenth header: bring it to the front of the row, then show its page.
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
expect fly.tabs.first 12
click fly-tab-tlogs
expect fly.tab tabTLogs
expect fly.page.overflow 0

# A log given as the link plays as LoadLogFile plays one: its name shown, playing, at 1x.
expect fly.playback.file autotest.tlog
expect fly.playback.playing true
expect fly.playback.button Pause
expect fly.playback.speed x 1

# 10x: what is left of the recording in under four seconds.
click fly-speed10
expect fly.playback.speed x 10

# The end of the file stops it, at 100%, with the button back to Play.
expect fly.playback.playing false
expect fly.playback.button Play
expect fly.playback.percent 100.00%
expect fly.playback.tracklog 100

# A press left of the thumb moves it one LargeChange back, and the file with it; still stopped.
click fly-tracklog@0.02x0.5
expect fly.playback.tracklog 95
expect fly.playback.percent ~ 95.
expect fly.playback.playing false

# The slowest speed, then Play: it plays from there - 1.8 recorded seconds at 0.1x is eighteen.
click fly-speed1_10
expect fly.playback.speed x 0.1
click fly-playlog
expect fly.playback.playing true
expect fly.playback.button Pause

# Pause holds it.
click fly-playlog
expect fly.playback.playing false
expect fly.playback.button Play
